Boltz-2 WebGPU — virtual screening in the browser
=================================================

This repository is a FORK. It is a clone of LocalFold at the pinned commit
below, with a Boltz-2 affinity module and a screening page added on top.

Upstream: LocalFold
-------------------
  https://github.com/sokrypton/localfold
  pinned commit 357518613af612b4e1e887deecd93bd612fdac76 (see notes/ and spec/)
  © Sergey Ovchinnikov, "THE BEER-WARE LICENSE" (Revision 42) — see LICENSE.

LocalFold's own README is kept verbatim as README-localfold.md rather than
overwritten, and its licence file is unchanged. Everything in this tree that is
not listed as new below is LocalFold's work: the WebGPU runtime, the AF3-lineage
trunk, diffusion and confidence stacks, the weight loaders and quantisation, the
featurisers, the SMILES chemistry, the page shell and the whole gate harness.

What is new in this fork
------------------------
Written for this project (see README.md, "What is reverse-engineered from
upstream Boltz", for what each one was derived from and how it is checked):

  screen.html, web/screen*.js        the screening page, its 3D scene, plot,
                                     CSV and ZIP export
  web/affinity-*.js                  the two-pass affinity run
  webgpu/af3/affinity/, cpu/af3/affinity/
                                     the affinity module: kernels and the
                                     float64 reference
  shared/af3/affinity/               the crop and featurisation
  shared/chem/canonical-rank.js, canon-partitions.js, canon-input.js
                                     RDKit's canonical atom ranking, ported
  tools/g0_verify.py, g8_compare.py, g8_localise.py,
  tools/export_boltz2_affinity.py, tools/oracle/dump_boltz2_*.py
                                     the checkpoint readers and the comparisons
                                     against upstream PyTorch Boltz-2

